Sampāti bathes after water rite and sits ringed on hill --- Sampāti bids silent attention promising truth about Maithilī --- Sampāti recalls sun-burnt fall and six-night swoon --- Sampāti surveys seas mountains and knows Vindhya --- Sampāti finds fragrant Niśākara āśram with unfailing trees --- Sampāti waits under tree for bathing north-facing sage --- Beasts honor sage then disperse like army before king --- Sage welcomes Sampāti and asks wing ruin --- Sage recalls brother vulture kings grasping his feet
